# Mainroom

Share subscription inference capacity with friends and research groups.
Each person gets one endpoint at https://<username>.mainroom.sh/v1, backed
by their own accounts and nodes shared with them. Providers control access
and usage limits.

[Website](https://mainroom.sh) · [Guides](https://mainroom.sh/guides) · [API reference](https://mainroom.sh/docs)

## Get started

[Download the CLI](https://github.com/cs50victor/mainroom/releases/latest),
extract it, and put mainroom on your PATH.

    mainroom auth signup
    mainroom codex sync

Sync uploads the local Codex credentials you select. To use a friend's capacity
or connect an inference client, follow the [setup guide](https://mainroom.sh/guides/getting-started).

## Account recovery

    mainroom codex status
    mainroom codex reauth --account <filename.json>
    mainroom codex disable <filename.json>

Reauth requires the official Codex CLI and preserves your usual local login.
Disable keeps the credential but stops the remote machine, interrupting active
requests. The remote machine runs tokenproxy; no local tokenproxy install is needed.

## Architecture

A Cloudflare Worker handles authentication, sharing, and routing to each user's
Fly Machine running tokenproxy. Durable Objects store machine and sharing state,
R2 stores credentials, Clerk handles sign-in, and a Bun/Hono container serves
the backend API.

For local setup, code reuse, test standards, and PR checks, see
[CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md).
